{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     custom-style-guide.hbs — the theme's own proof sheet.
     Type scale from NSDS templates/type-specimen.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     A Ghost custom template: make a page, pick "Style guide" in the editor.

     ── WHAT A STYLE GUIDE IS FOR HERE, AND WHY IT IS TWO HALVES ────────────
     The theme's job is Ghost's content model wearing NSDS's clothes, so the
     two things that can be wrong are (a) an NSDS token drifting and (b) a
     Ghost element nobody styled. This page shows both, and the halves are
     built differently ON PURPOSE:

     · The SPECIMEN half is markup in this file, because the type scale is
       the theme's claim about itself and must not depend on someone
       remembering to write it in an editor.

     · The PROSE half is {{content}} — the page's own body. It cannot be
       hard-coded: the whole question it answers is "what does GHOST's
       output look like here", and Ghost's output comes from Koenig. Paste
       one of every card into the page — heading, list, quote, code, table,
       bookmark, callout, toggle, gallery — and this is where they are
       checked. A hard-coded imitation of Koenig's markup would prove only
       that the imitation is styled.

     ⚠ gh-content AND ns-prose, both. .gh-content is what theme/ghost.css
     scopes its Koenig overrides to; without it Ghost's own cards.min.css
     wins and every card renders as a white box on the navy surface. The
     long version is in page.hbs.

     ── LOOK AT IT IN BOTH THEMES ───────────────────────────────────────────
     abstract/collections.md's build list ends with "looked at — in both
     themes, at 360px, with JavaScript off", because gscan and a green build
     have both been green on a visually broken site. This is the page to do
     that on.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
{{#post}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner ns-stack">
        <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "// Proof sheet"}}</span>
        <h1 class="ns-display">{{#if title}}{{title}}{{else}}{{t "Style guide"}}{{/if}}</h1>
        {{#if custom_excerpt}}<p class="ns-band__lede">{{custom_excerpt}}</p>{{/if}}
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── The type scale ───────────────────────────────────────────────── --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--sunken ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner ns-stack">
        <span class="ns-label">{{t "Type scale"}}</span>
        <p class="ns-display ns-display--mega">Aa</p>
        <h1>{{t "Heading one"}}</h1>
        <h2>{{t "Heading two"}}</h2>
        <h3>{{t "Heading three"}}</h3>
        <p class="ns-measure">{{t "Body copy sits on a measure of roughly 68 characters, because a line the full width of a wide screen is the fastest way to make good writing unreadable. This paragraph is here to be measured, not read."}}</p>
        <p><a class="ns-link" href="#">{{t "A link in running text"}}</a></p>
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── The chrome the theme draws around content ─────────────────────── --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner ns-stack">
        <span class="ns-label">{{t "Components"}}</span>
        <div class="ns-cluster">
            <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary" href="#">{{t "Primary"}}</a>
            <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline" href="#">{{t "Outline"}}</a>
            <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--quiet" href="#">{{t "Quiet"}}</a>
            <span class="ns-tag">{{t "Tag"}}</span>
            <span class="ns-status ns-status--success">{{t "Status"}}</span>
        </div>
        {{> "empty" title=(t "And this is an empty state") text=(t "Every listing in the theme falls back to it.")}}
    </div>
</section>

{{!-- ── Ghost's own output, styled ────────────────────────────────────── --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <span class="ns-label">{{t "Ghost content"}}</span>
        <div class="gh-content ns-prose">{{content}}</div>
    </div>
</section>
{{/post}}
